<title>UK: Yorkshire, Southern up on renewed bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire, Southern up on renewed bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yorkshire Electricity and Southern Electric shares jumped as Entergy Power's agreed bid to buy London Electricity reignited bid hopes in the British regional electricity sector, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0904 GMT, shares in Yorkshire added 17p to 772-1/2p, while shares in Southern climbed 13-1/2p to 781p.  </p>
<p>Meanwhile, shares in London Electricity rose 4p to 687-1/2p after it agreed to a 1.3 billion stg bid from Entergy.</p>
<p>The move comes after the UK government on Friday cleared the hostile bid for Northern Electricity Plc from U.S. utility CE Electric</p>
<p>Southern and Yorkshire are now the only two remaining Recs which are not currently subject to bids.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
